# Zone's deployment settings. Copy to .env (cp .env.example .env) and edit;
# .env is gitignored. Every setting is optional except ZONE_DATA. Uncomment a
# line to use it. Details: docs/spec/deployment.md.
#
# The wiki's own settings (a password or users, the MCP token, hosts, locale,
# sharing mode …) are in the wiki's settings file, .zone/config, which Zone
# reloads without a restart: ./run.sh config passwd, ./run.sh user add alice,
# or edit it. See docs/spec/users.md.

# The wiki folder, which must exist (default ~/zonewiki). run.sh expands a ~.
# Used without run.sh, give an absolute path.
ZONE_DATA=~/zonewiki

# Timezone, so "today" is your day (default: the host's, via run.sh; else UTC).
# TZ=Europe/Berlin

# Network access: 1 listens on the LAN (e.g. for your phone), default localhost
# only. Without hosts in the settings file (the names Zone may be reached by
# besides localhost), any name reaches it then.
# ZONE_ALLOW_REMOTE=1

# Semantic search with a local model, baked in at build (adds about 1 GB).
# ZONE_SEMANTIC_SEARCH=on

# Only for docker compose without run.sh (run.sh sets these itself):
# ZONE_BIND=0.0.0.0
# ZONE_UID=1000
# ZONE_GID=1000

# compose.nas.yaml (the prebuilt image on a NAS or server) also needs
# ZONE_DATA as an absolute path and ZONE_UID/ZONE_GID of the wiki folder's
# owner. The port on the host, default 5080 (Synology's DSM has 5000):
# ZONE_PORT=5080
